From 700ee41fe451829ebde5193d7c66d033a8e01cd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RNVizion <vizionaryfx@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 19:11:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] mix_colors enforces the 12-color limit its description
 has always published

The tool description, the README and the Runbook have said "up to 12
colors" since Phase 0; the code accepted any count. A documented limit the
code does not enforce means a caller who reads the description and one
who does not get different servers. Now a thirteenth color is refused
with the count and a remedy (mix in stages), checked before any color is
resolved so the structural problem surfaces first.

Enforcing rather than dropping the claim: the published contract is the
promise, the limit comes from the desktop mixer's slot count, and the
locked scope widens only on demand already in evidence -- none exists.

- api.py: MAX_MIX_COLORS = 12, with the reason at the definition.
- tests/test_input_limits.py (4): positive control at exactly the limit;
  refusal names limit and count; count checked before resolution; the
  description's number is read from server.py and held equal to the
  constant, so moving one without the other fails.

Both halves broken deliberately (check removed; description changed to
10) and each failed for its named reason. Suite 86 -> 90.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01McgAPxvtUNHD5Z46jfvF3o
