Subject: [PATCH 2/3] smoke scripts can no longer write to the production
 Dataset; server_test covers ten tools

Both hand-run smoke scripts built the palette store from whatever HF_TOKEN
was in the environment. A Codespace carries an HF_TOKEN secret, so running
either one there would hydrate from the production Dataset and push test
palettes back over it -- "Spring line" first -- to the extent that token
has Dataset write access. Not observed (production's "Spring line" is not
a smoke value); the path was live. The pytest suite was always safe:
tests/conftest.py strips the token. The scripts now do the same, before
`api` or `server` is imported, and assert the store holds no token before
anything is saved.

The setup runs only under __main__ and the environment-dependent imports
moved inside main(): pytest's default glob matches *_test.py, so both
modules are imported at collection, and mutating the environment there
would rebuild the server auth-off under test_auth and test_scopes.

- tests/server_test.py: isolated; EXPECTED_TOOLS gains place_lightness
  (the README's "exercises all tools" was failing on a nine-tool set);
  exercises place_lightness against the register's blue pair and
  list_palettes; mixes red + yellow rather than red + blue, since "blue"
  is RNV blue; the closing count is derived.
- tests/smoke_test.py: isolated; checks place_lightness; the red + blue
  mix now says css:blue and asserts bare "blue" is RNV blue.
- .gitignore: palettes.json, the store path a local `python server.py`
  writes when RNV_PALETTE_STORE is unset.

Verified with a fake HF_TOKEN planted in the environment: both scripts
strip it and write nothing to the repo root. Tampered (strip removed),
both refuse with the named assertion before any save. Suite 90 on 3.12
and 3.13, collection unaffected.

