From ca1cd80accebf939d8eb932d66e49c49e1d75970 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RNVizion <vizionaryfx@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 19:18:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] public surfaces describe the server that exists, and a
 test holds them to it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two weeks after the tenth tool landed, five surfaces still described nine
or fewer: the README's tool table and auth paragraph, SECURITY.md's scope,
a comment in server.py, and api.py's header and __all__. Each was right
the day it was written; describers stay behind when the thing they
describe moves (practices §7.6, §3.2.2).

Corrections:
- README: place_lightness in the table; "every read-only tool" for the
  read scope; the "color engine is not under automated test" sentence
  replaced by what the suite pins and what it does not, with no count
  (principle 3: the badge carries the number); "Identifiers are local by
  design" removed, retired by the register 2026-08-17 and surviving here
  outside the mirror guard's reach (§4.3); the brand/CSS collision set
  named (gold, blue, teal) with css:blue as the escape; the persistence
  bullet says saves land in the local working copy and report
  durable/durable_reason; the smoke commands no longer promise a count.
- README "Try it": "Mix paint-red and paint-blue" now resolved blue to
  RNV blue and returned #8c0000, a dark red. Replaced with crimson +
  royalblue (paint #5d2157, a plum, L* 24 against 40 in rgb). Written
  royalblue as one word because aliases are not normalized: "royal blue"
  refuses today (parked).
- SECURITY.md, server.py comment, api.py header: counts removed rather
  than updated -- "eight" was correct once too. api.py __all__ gains the
  three tools it was missing.
- server.py instructions (model-facing): now name placement and
  measurement, the collision set with blue's two values, and that unknown
  names, schemes and operations are refused.
- mix_colors description (model-facing) and the Kubelka-Munk docstring:
  paint works per RGB channel, reflectance clamped at 0.001, so an empty
  channel dominates -- #ffff00 + #0000ff -> #000000, red + yellow ->
  #fe0000, white + #0000ff -> #0000fe. The docstring promised "Yellow +
  Blue = Green"; for those inputs it was false. ryb gives #007f00. Stated,
  not fixed: a better pigment model is Phase 7 engine work.
- server.json: "place" added to the registry description (99 of the
  schema's 100 characters). Reaches the registry on the next tag.

tests/test_public_surfaces.py (36): the tool set is discovered from
server.py with ast and the README table, api.__all__ and api's header are
held equal to it; six surfaces are swept for spelled tool counts (the
pattern carries the noun and cannot cross punctuation); the retired
rationale is absent; the collision set named in the README equals the
set the engine computes, and the instructions name each key and blue's
two values; every paint figure the prose quotes is asserted (a
limitation pinned, so improving the model fails here and forces the text
to move with it); server.json fits the registry's 100-character limit.
Positive controls for the discovery, the count sweep in both directions,
and the instructions reader -- whose first version split on "),", stopped
inside a parenthesis, and was replaced by an ast read.

Verified: each pre-8.1 surface restored in turn fails by name (README
five ways, SECURITY.md, api.py three ways, server.py four ways); a
101+-character description fails; changing the paint clamp fails the
four collapse figures. Suite 90 -> 126 on 3.12 and 3.13.

